# 1. Canadian Pipeline Code – CSA Z662

## Location Classes

- Z662 is the Canadian pipeline code.
- The code establishes different pipeline location classes:
    - **Class 1:** Wilderness areas.
    - **Class 4:** High-rise / densely populated areas.
- When a pipeline is built, builders must take into account the current location class of each section.
- The reason for having different location classes is that pipelines are pressure-containing entities:
    - Higher location classes require thicker pipeline walls.
- Future development must also be taken into account to predict where housing may be built.

**Example:**

- ATCO could have built a pipeline 40 years ago.
- Very old pipelines can experience location class changes that did not exist when they were originally built.
- Pipeline companies regularly track their pipelines to make sure they are up to date with current requirements.
- A lot of planning is involved in accounting for these changes.

